{"name":"Blue Heaven","hex":"#5b7e98","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue heaven","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A capsule or tablet of amobarbital."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue_heaven"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blue Heaven (1994 TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Blue Heaven is a British television sitcom that starred Frank Skinner, Conleth Hill, John Forgeham, Nadim Sawalha and Paula Wilcox. It featured guest stars such as Bill Bailey, Bob Goody, Tamsin Greig, Lucy Davis, Beryl Reid, Philip Glenister and John Thomson."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Heaven_(1994_TV_series)","wikidata":"Q4929192"},{"title":"Blue Heaven (2003 TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Blue Heaven is a Scottish television documentary series filmed by BBC Scotland which followed aspiring young footballers at Rangers Football Club as they tried to forge a career in football. The series was originally broadcast in the winter of 2003 with a follow-up episode in 2011."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Heaven_(2003_TV_series)","wikidata":"Q4929190"},{"title":"Blue Heaven (flavour)","blocks":[{"text":"Blue Heaven is a milkshake and topping flavour sold primarily in Australia. It is blue in colour, and its taste is most commonly described as a mix of vanilla and raspberry, although its exact flavour is not fixed and varies between manufacturers and products. Sometimes it is marketed as a \"Blue Moon\" milkshake."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Blue_heaven_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Blue_heaven_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Heaven_(flavour)","wikidata":"Q48804759"},{"title":"Heaven","blocks":[{"text":"Heaven, or the Heavens, is a common religious cosmological or supernatural place where beings such as deities, angels, souls, saints, or venerated ancestors are said to originate, be enthroned, or reside. According to the beliefs of some religions, heavenly beings can descend to Earth or incarnate and earthly beings can ascend to Heaven in the afterlife or, in exceptional cases, enter Heaven without dying."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Paradiso_Canto_31_%28148200393%29.jpg/330px-Paradiso_Canto_31_%28148200393%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heaven","wikidata":"Q4489450"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Blue_Heaven_milkshake_and_flavour_syrup.jpg/500px-Blue_Heaven_milkshake_and_flavour_syrup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Blue_Heaven_milkshake_and_flavour_syrup.jpg/1280px-Blue_Heaven_milkshake_and_flavour_syrup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Blue_Heaven_milkshake_and_flavour_syrup.jpg/500px-Blue_Heaven_milkshake_and_flavour_syrup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Blue Heaven milkshake and flavour syrup from a beachside Kiosk in Semaphore, South Australia. ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlue_Heaven_milkshake_and_flavour_syrup.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/86/Beowulf_-_heofones.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/86/Beowulf_-_heofones.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"\"heofones\", an ancient Anglo-Saxon word for heavens in Beowulf","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABeowulf_-_heofones.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Ruins_from_a_temple_in_Naffur.jpg/500px-Ruins_from_a_te